{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0e4251a539d939fbb92dc47c02dc4634ab606aba944ff261b394f5dd12078a26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Trajectories persist in a Turso (SQLite) store defaulting to ~/.sondera/trajectories/trajectories.db, overridable via --db; the console reads agents and trajectories from the same store."},{"claim_ids":["clm_282c65fb898dbc36c04ca741468f17d4fe306b35cfe25c16f96733339b435d11"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Enabling the LLM classifiers adds latency to every decision they touch, and with guardrails enabled event content is sent to the configured provider."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3a741e09d77fec14ba60d2e5a9ae0b274fa33b27303aa30df5d27b2d97db7b71"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The optional LLM classifiers fail open when disabled, erroring, or slower than the adjudication budget — to compliant with no violations and to Public — so Cedar and the deterministic policies still decide."},{"claim_ids":["clm_62c117de4ded26410eb724f0fcc8271166c43e9219430589de5e69647fb51b55"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The signature engine and Cedar policies run with no external dependencies or API keys; the optional LLM classifiers support Ollama (the default when enabled), OpenAI-compatible servers, Anthropic, Gemini, and Vertex AI via Application Default Credentials."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0e4251a539d939fbb92dc47c02dc4634ab606aba944ff261b394f5dd12078a26","clm_282c65fb898dbc36c04ca741468f17d4fe306b35cfe25c16f96733339b435d11","clm_3a741e09d77fec14ba60d2e5a9ae0b274fa33b27303aa30df5d27b2d97db7b71","clm_62c117de4ded26410eb724f0fcc8271166c43e9219430589de5e69647fb51b55"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:24Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f0ec349a8ce4f3a950726d28a52970a","id":"pg_13e9e3f513c45edfae7ad91df73d6637","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sondera-ai-sondera-coding-agent-hooks-docs-configuration-md-9efefedd24-d91df73d6637.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_d86caacffeb959b98224e809250edad0"],"title":"sondera-ai/sondera-coding-agent-hooks/docs/configuration.md @ 9efefedd249e","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:24Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f0ec349a8ce4f3a950726d28a52970a"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2e75df0423716b7eb4c091eb3655c1c73464b5c8c6790a97c2d6d57a61e9f4d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The harness coordinates three guardrail subsystems: a YARA-X signature engine (always on and the only deterministic one), an optional LLM secure-code policy classifier, and optional LLM information-flow sensitivity labeling."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3a741e09d77fec14ba60d2e5a9ae0b274fa33b27303aa30df5d27b2d97db7b71"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The optional LLM classifiers fail open when disabled, erroring, or slower than the adjudication budget — to compliant with no violations and to Public — so Cedar and the deterministic policies still decide."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7783327bc069eb34f4f2ce168fe6716dc241982bfa659502336eedb6607d1c86"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent execution is modeled as a trajectory of typed events in four categories: Action (pre-execution), Observation (post-execution), Control (lifecycle), and State (environment snapshots)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8767f500c0ffa2ddd79be00717321c6c9125448995e9b94ae40097ee222889ef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Cedar policy engine combines guardrail signals with entity state from a Turso (SQLite) local store and returns Allow, Deny, or Escalate adjudications back through the hook adapter."},{"claim_ids":["clm_88ed8a71d007983c82e9c01c87da37e888b9248facff52d23c5abc89708dd93d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent-specific tool names normalize to shared event types (Claude's Bash, Cursor's shell hook, Copilot's and Gemini's bash all become ShellCommand), so one Cedar rule set governs every supported agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bf8497c681173ea7473cce5d7575717ec448844610374f088825240865108883"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hook adapters speak stdin/stdout JSON with each agent, normalize the payload, and forward it over gRPC to `sondera serve` on loopback TCP, 127.0.0.1:50051 by default."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2e75df0423716b7eb4c091eb3655c1c73464b5c8c6790a97c2d6d57a61e9f4d5","clm_3a741e09d77fec14ba60d2e5a9ae0b274fa33b27303aa30df5d27b2d97db7b71","clm_7783327bc069eb34f4f2ce168fe6716dc241982bfa659502336eedb6607d1c86","clm_8767f500c0ffa2ddd79be00717321c6c9125448995e9b94ae40097ee222889ef","clm_88ed8a71d007983c82e9c01c87da37e888b9248facff52d23c5abc89708dd93d","clm_bf8497c681173ea7473cce5d7575717ec448844610374f088825240865108883"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:24Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f0ec349a8ce4f3a950726d28a52970a","id":"pg_41a7ecf183b85ccdb377c988d08a8fd0","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sondera-ai-sondera-coding-agent-hooks-docs-architecture-md-9efefedd249-c988d08a8fd0.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_01675cc58c7b54a0b51e577833b380da"],"title":"sondera-ai/sondera-coding-agent-hooks/docs/architecture.md @ 9efefedd249e","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:24Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f0ec349a8ce4f3a950726d28a52970a"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0e4251a539d939fbb92dc47c02dc4634ab606aba944ff261b394f5dd12078a26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Trajectories persist in a Turso (SQLite) store defaulting to ~/.sondera/trajectories/trajectories.db, overridable via --db; the console reads agents and trajectories from the same store."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7f7b6605c571d369fa524101d1df8ae9f1b2a6d10f929c62895d4780b44a69ef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`sondera serve` runs two gRPC surfaces on one address: `sondera.harness.v1` for Cedar-backed adjudication and `sondera.console.v1` for agent and trajectory reads over the same store."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0e4251a539d939fbb92dc47c02dc4634ab606aba944ff261b394f5dd12078a26","clm_7f7b6605c571d369fa524101d1df8ae9f1b2a6d10f929c62895d4780b44a69ef"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:24Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f0ec349a8ce4f3a950726d28a52970a","id":"pg_44aeb3da09bd5e8491d69f8b9bb4fb2d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sondera-ai-sondera-coding-agent-hooks-docs-getting-started-md-9efefedd-9f8b9bb4fb2d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f0da4b17648057c28619e11006e8f9cf"],"title":"sondera-ai/sondera-coding-agent-hooks/docs/getting-started.md @ 9efefedd249e","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:24Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f0ec349a8ce4f3a950726d28a52970a"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0e4251a539d939fbb92dc47c02dc4634ab606aba944ff261b394f5dd12078a26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Trajectories persist in a Turso (SQLite) store defaulting to ~/.sondera/trajectories/trajectories.db, overridable via --db; the console reads agents and trajectories from the same store."},{"claim_ids":["clm_151be13f17087c676c76c50fa013810f91a0db8e8fd85e1e01d7c53462f871c4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: integration tests needing a reachable model provider are #[ignore]d by default and run explicitly with `cargo test -- --ignored` once the configured provider is up."},{"claim_ids":["clm_27d771a4615fbcfb0f831dc6ebc3d807780d2876177289fb5125954e43a0c26f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: CI runs cargo fmt --check, clippy with -D warnings, cargo doc, cargo test --locked --workspace, cargo deny check, and buf lint/format from crates/schema/proto; working conventions live in AGENTS.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_58dec173115ed2b423be7154e433283dda251967e8fda2d4f71ff19d60f81761"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every hook adapter depends on the harness crate as sondera-harness-client with default-features off and only the client feature, linking the gRPC client but not the policy engine."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0e4251a539d939fbb92dc47c02dc4634ab606aba944ff261b394f5dd12078a26","clm_151be13f17087c676c76c50fa013810f91a0db8e8fd85e1e01d7c53462f871c4","clm_27d771a4615fbcfb0f831dc6ebc3d807780d2876177289fb5125954e43a0c26f","clm_58dec173115ed2b423be7154e433283dda251967e8fda2d4f71ff19d60f81761"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:24Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f0ec349a8ce4f3a950726d28a52970a","id":"pg_8a00673dd9a55fb7821d518c4f6e7819","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sondera-ai-sondera-coding-agent-hooks-docs-development-md-9efefedd249e-518c4f6e7819.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_e361bf4545be5159945eb84b83b5c0a7"],"title":"sondera-ai/sondera-coding-agent-hooks/docs/development.md @ 9efefedd249e","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:22:24Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f0ec349a8ce4f3a950726d28a52970a"}
